cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Junoview in your work, please cite it."
title: "Junoview"
abstract: >-
  Figure-first viewing of executed Jupyter notebooks, plus a slide-deck
  builder. A single-file, standard-library-only tool that recovers the
  scientific structure of a run notebook and renders it as a navigable,
  figure-first document with a live provenance graph — and builds
  presentations from the same cells.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Alex"
    family-names: "Borowiak"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: add your ORCID
    affiliation: "University of Leeds"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexborowiak/semantic-rendering"  # TODO: update if the repo is renamed to junoview
url: "https://plotline-nb.dev"  # TODO: update to the junoview domain once live
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - jupyter
  - notebook
  - visualization
  - presentation
  - xarray
  - reproducibility
